# Class declaration with injective: true (a VarRef, not Int) silently treated as non-injective.
# Per parser.rs: the injective field is only read when SurfaceExpression::Int is present.
# A VarRef like `true` does not match that arm, so resolver_injective defaults to false.
# No parse or type error is emitted — the class simply behaves as non-injective.
[
  TestClass: [class [let TestClass a b c]
    [determines: [[[a b] c]]
     resolver: TestResolver
     injective: true]
    test: [Fn@c [a b]]]

  result: "ok"
]
---
%.result
=== out
String("ok")
